{
  "id": "symbol-grounding",
  "term": "symbol grounding",
  "definition": "Symbol grounding is the problem of how a symbol comes to have meaning, especially how numerical symbols gain their numerical meaning. In this context, proposed explanations include linking symbols to nonverbal quantity representations or building meaning through relations among symbols themselves.",
